{"type":"standard","title":"J. D. Ford","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">J. D. Ford</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q58755278","titles":{"canonical":"J._D._Ford","normalized":"J. D. Ford","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">J. D. Ford</span></span>"},"pageid":59049057,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/JD_Ford%2C_Indy_Pride_Parade_2023_%282%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-JD_Ford%2C_Indy_Pride_Parade_2023_%282%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","width":330,"height":431},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/JD_Ford%2C_Indy_Pride_Parade_2023_%282%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":381,"height":498},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1372251598","tid":"ab0ee727-a4d7-11f1-91e4-f32bb6e0a4b2","timestamp":"2026-08-31T01:02:42Z","description":"American politician","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J._D._Ford","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J._D._Ford?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J._D._Ford?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:J._D._Ford"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J._D._Ford","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/J._D._Ford","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J._D._Ford?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:J._D._Ford"}},"extract":"J. D. Ford is an American politician, currently a member of the Indiana Senate. Elected in the 2018 elections, he represents Senate District 29 as a member of the Democratic Party. He earned a bachelor's degree from University of Akron in criminal justice and political science and a master's degree in education from Purdue University Northwest. He is the Democratic nominee for Indiana's 5th congressional district in 2026, and will face Republican incumbent Victoria Spartz in the general election.","extract_html":"<p><b>J. D. Ford</b> is an American politician, currently a member of the Indiana Senate. Elected in the 2018 elections, he represents Senate District 29 as a member of the Democratic Party. He earned a bachelor's degree from University of Akron in criminal justice and political science and a master's degree in education from Purdue University Northwest. He is the Democratic nominee for Indiana's 5th congressional district in 2026, and will face Republican incumbent Victoria Spartz in the general election.</p>"}